WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:31.420 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  us  humans have dominated the planet for  millennia  residing comfortably at the top of the  food chain  we pride ourselves with our technology  built  walls to shield us from the dangers  lurking outside  we cultivate and shape nature  manipulated  to fulfill our needs and from the safety  and comfort of our territories  we gaze upon the beauty of nature from  afar  from a distance the vast landscapes of  hyrule  are stunning serene calming even  but looks can be deceiving strip away  the comforts of our civilization  and the average hylian will soon find  out the hardships  of surviving in the wild out here  instinct and knowledge of the land  dictate the chances of survival  which resources are valuable or safe for  consumption  and which are better left untouched how  to brave the diverse and harsh climates  and perhaps more importantly how to  interact with the many creatures  roaming the wastes hyrule is absolutely  brimming with life  from the smallest of rodents to the  majestic wild horses of the plain  wolf packs bonded together in search for  prey  the intimidating and fierce grizzly bear  some friendly some hostile all  living in harmony with their environment  [Music]  but there is something else living here  as well  a species which stands out from the rest  of the animal kingdom  due to a general higher intelligence  coordination  and thus intimidation factor so much so  that they are classified in a category  of their own  separate from the other wildlife you and  i  know them as monsters fitting really  it's a term often used by us humans to  describe  something we don't fully understand  something  vile or cruel which sparks fear  and seemingly operates with no  conscience or emotion  savage primitive but is that truly the  full picture  or is there more to these critters than  meets the eye  perhaps misunderstood even today we take  a closer look at one such creature  a familiar face found in every corner of  hyrule  from the highest of mountains to the  grassy plains of nicuda  the bokoblin for the last weeks  we have studied these beings extensively  from a safe distance  analyze their behavioral patterns  traditions  and interactions with their surroundings  bokoblins  are naturally hostile to humans cross  their paths will get in the way of their  prey  and they won't hesitate to use brute  force  amongst their own kind and even other  species of monsters however  they are very much social creatures like  ourselves  it is extraordinarily rare to encounter  a lone bokoblin  on your travels rather they prefer to  operate in groups or tribes  making them even harder to approach or  interact with  like us they have realized the concept  of strength in numbers  but we need to learn more taking notes  and spying on them from a safe distance  doesn't grant us a true and honest  insight into their true nature  in order to truly understand the  bulgoblin we must attempt to make  contact  live like them and learn the nature of  their ways  through close interaction but how  their hostility towards our species  serves as roadblock to conduct a proper  study  that is why in the lead-up to our quest  for knowledge  we have devised a strategy to overcome  the barriers separating us from them  using the latest in stealth technology  we have conducted a clever disguise  based on our current understanding of  the creature  one which hopefully will allow us to  fool our subjects  into accepting us as one of their own  but  looks aren't everything of course body  language is equally as important  to achieve our goal of blending in  notice  the hunched over starts arms stretched  out to the side  to mimic the neutral position of the  bokoblin  this is an essential part of the  disguise  break character and one might risk the  disguise falling apart  of which the consequences could be dire  all that is left now is to wait for the  break of dawn  as tomorrow we put our strategy to the  ultimate test  [Music]  sunrise a new day dawns in hyrule  and we are ready to start our research  for our experiment we have chosen the  great plateau  as the most viable location its secluded  nature  acts as its own little ecosystem  separate from the rest of land  bokoblin's camps are plentiful in this  area  some small some large some seek shelter  while others prefer to sleep under the  stars  our target is this camp right here up on  the ridge  close to the ruins of the temple of time  it's one of the medium-sized camps out  here  consisting of a total of three  inhabitants tucked away  on this remote cliffside a perfect way  to study our subjects undisturbed  carefully we make our approach please  remember  that this is a high risk operation  performed by a trained professional  thus we must insist that one does not  attempt this on their own  it seems the bokoblins have spotted us  this is the moment of truth so far so  good  no signs of hostility yet instead  fascination and curiosity reign supreme  who is this stranger crossing into our  domain  why is he here after some careful  assessment  the bokoblins returned to their daily  routine  seemingly unfazed by their otherworldly  visitor  the disguise works but we are far from  getting accepted into their ranks  right away we notice a hierarchy within  the clan  notice the dark grey skin tone and the  war paint on the body of this particular  specimen  a clear sign that he is calling the  shots around here  the other two rotate shifts fulfilling  their duties in service of the tribe  hunting guard duty cooking  it's a fascinating display of teamwork  really  one of the first things we learn is that  bokoblins  don't seem to bother with names well not  vocally anyway for convenience sake  we've decided to assign each their own  name  to avoid confusion grey their chief in  command  red and larry  that night we weren't allowed to sleep  at the campfire  gray simply wouldn't allow it who can  blame them really  in their eyes we are an intruder  a strange and unusual visitor from  foreign lands  in general the different tribes living  on the plateau  don't seem to interact much they mostly  stick to their own kind  respecting each other's territory it's  something hyrule's developed races  could take notes from our histories are  rich  with the desire to expand our lands  to take it by any means necessary even  by force  bokoblins don't seem to share this lust  for power  as long as there's food on the table a  place to sleep  and companionship they are content to  live simple  lives out here in the wild tomorrow  we must find a way to win the hearts of  the tribe  and gain the trust of their leadership  let's hope our attempt is fruitful  at the break of dawn while the others  are out hunting  we gather some materials as a show of  goodwill to the tribe  mushrooms fruits and anything else the  land has to offer  hopefully this gesture will ease their  minds a bit  food has apparently been scarce as of  late  and today the hunting party once again  returns empty-handed upon laying eyes on  our offering  the group seems rather hesitant at first  but  quickly realizes that any food is better  than nothing at this point  despite our gift grey still seems  suspicious of us  however larry has seemingly opened up to  us a bit  as we indulged in some brief  conversation  at night we were even allowed to stay  for a while  and join in on the chitchat of course  their language is not one we currently  understand so some nods and some basic  hand signals will have to do  for now but alas one offering won't  reward us a spot at the warm campfire  just yet  and we've returned to our secluded  sleeping spot  under the trees to get some  well-deserved rest  for the next few days we repeat the same  daily routine  of looking after the camp while the  others are out hunting  we gather up materials polish and repair  weaponry  cook up some basic food and try to keep  the campsite clean  we continue to bond with our new found  friend  and we even got to join larry on guard  duty  which was a nice change of pace from the  usual busy work  at night we routinely join the group for  some small talk  until we are once again sent back to our  usual spot  as the outsider we still are until  one morning we are woken up by none  other than  grey who offers us to join the hunting  party today  it seems our hard work has finally paid  off  with almost a week without a successful  hunt the situation is getting more dire  and it seems even grey realizes they  will all need the help they can get  this might be our chance to finally  prove ourselves  as not to lose daylight we immediately  set out for the nearby forest  the ball roaming these woods have  dwindled in numbers  and are more skittish than ever before  making them harder and harder to catch  in order to cover more ground the group  decided to split up  gray and red try their luck up north  while larry  joins us as we continue westward into  the dense  forest maukoblins have found many  different ways to hunt their prey  some resort to a stealthy approach while  others  give chase and try to corner their prey  like a pack of wolves  some have even been seen riding various  animals  to take advantage of their speed they  craft their own weaponry  like wooden bows shields clubs and  spears  and although simplistic and primitive in  design  they get the job done when it comes to  survival in the wild  the fact that they are able to tame  wildlife and craft  weapons shows that they are far more  evolved than many had initially guessed  but we must keep our focus on the task  ahead  if we managed to bring home something  good  we might finally be accepted into the  tribe  so far the hunt has been fruitless  larry decides to search along the  cliffside  while we wander deeper into the forest  it looks like this might again turn into  a failed hunt  until finally a wild boar rears its head  amongst the tall grass this is it  our one chance  [Music]  [Music]  do  that night we feasted after weeks of no  success  this meal came as a gift from the  heavens  the mood of the tribe that night is one  of great joy and celebration  larry and red express their thanks and  even grey  seems to have changed his tone for the  better our many days of hard labor  bonding discipline and today's triumph  has earned us a spot at the campfire  gone are the days  of being an exile in the days ahead we  continue to hunt  gather converse and bond with this  fascinating species  the tribe's acceptance is a reward in  and of itself  but what really matters is the data  we've collected during  our journey unfortunately this is also  where our paths must diverge as much as  we've enjoyed our time with our  newfound friends we must return to our  own kind it's only a matter of time  until one day  they may find out who we really are  saying goodbye is something they  probably won't understand  it's a human thing after all instead  we shall slip away quietly into the  night  and hope that the tribe will understand  our decision  who knows we might meet again someday  perhaps we may even be able to make  contact without the use of disguises and  deception but for now our adventure  ends here  our research has shown that despite  their more primitive and simplistic  lifestyle the bokoblins have earned the  right to roam these lands  for centuries they have adapted and used  their exceptional survival skills  to thrive and while they are still  hostile to us  humans can we really blame them  monsters we call them but perhaps from  their perspective  we are the monsters here disturbing the  peace and crossing into their territory  without a care  for anything other than ourselves the  various tribes  living here respect each other's  boundaries they don't go to war with one  another  over territory or fight amongst  themselves  they have their own language culture  customs  and traditions they hunt and tame  wildlife  and craft tools like we do though  outshined by our intellect and  technology  there is still plenty to be learned from  the creatures roaming the wild  and perhaps one day we might be able to  establish a more friendly relationship  with them  if we put our prejudice aside  [Music]  one  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  you

